+| DR1 — child ownership/recovery | **Resolved at design level** | The `run.py` interface now has synchronous `observe(ProcessObservation)` in addition to `env`; `Event` persists lifecycle facts. `procedures.process_recovery` explicitly preserves the spawn-to-record uncertainty, treats direct-child exit as insufficient for descendant death, and blocks unsupported recovery. Observer-write failure triggers only best-effort cleanup and unresolved admission, never a false success. Live-child, missing-observation and callback-failure cases are specified. This meets the accepted conservative alternative: no imaginary process visibility, guaranteed orphan cleanup, reset API or automatic replay. |
